WEBVTT

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:47.280
One, two, three...

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.040
Lavender!

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:53.710
It's freezing!

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.070
Even mornings in Hokkaido are cold.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:00:59.880
No...

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:02.050
Someone, somewhere,

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:04.800
just did something chilling.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.590
Morning! Did you guys just wake up?

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.120
Hane... You're up pretty early.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:10.700
Eh?

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:13.320
Well, I just went to the flower fields.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.770
Ah, so you went to the bathroom?

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:35.280
この坂を上り切ったら
kono saka o noborikittara

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.240
必ず見える景色が好きだって
kanarazu mieru keshiki ga suki datte

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:39.280
必ず見える景色が好きだって

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.410
背中に羽を持つあの子も言って笑ってた
senaka ni hane o motsu ano ko mo itte waratteta

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:49.080
ドキドキが一瞬で
dokidoki ga isshun de

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:53.170
トキメキになっていくんだなんて
tokimeki ni natteikunda nante

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:56.880
あの頃は信じられなくて
ano koro wa shinjirarenakute

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.850
ただ見惚れていたよ
tada mitoreteita yo

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.480
このスピードに乗せた体温が
kono supiido ni noseta taion ga

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.230
今全身で伝う　通じ合う
ima zenshin de tsutau tsuujiau

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.860
物語の鍵はこの手に
monogatari no kagi wa kono te ni

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:17.360
ぎゅっと強く握っているから
gyutto tsuyoku nigitteiru kara

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.070
感じて　応えて　風になる
kanjite kotaete kaze ni naru

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.740
空に溶けて海を抱きしめる
sora ni tokete umi o dakishimeru

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:28.660
新しい世界が見えるはず
atarashii sekai ga mieru hazu

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:35.760
さぁ確かめに行ってみよう
saa tashikame ni ittemiyou

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.640
Touring!!
Episode 5

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:48.980
Well then, let's eat.
Touring!!
Episode 5

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.190
Well then, let's eat.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:54.520
Why even camp if we're gonna
eat convenience store food?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.730
Oh my lord, this nori is very crisp.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.320
What an amazing mechanism.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.990
I bought them at the Seicomart again.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:05.410
Just like how the monkey king in
<i>Journey to the West</i>

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.450
couldn't escape from Buddha,

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:11.250
as long as we're in Hokkaido,
we'll never escape the Seicomarts.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:13.920
Something like this?

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.290
What's this?!

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.050
We are such renegades.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:20.430
Onsa-chan, this is a bit too skimpy.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.350
Well, in a way, it's the most
Hokkaido-like the food can get.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.770
This reminds me,

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:32.850
cars in Hokkaido go really fast, don't they?

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.230
That was surprising.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.730
Yeah, everyone drives 1.25 times
the speed of the mainland.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.740
I have heard stories of Hokkaido police
chasing speeders with those helicopters.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.120
No way.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:45.830
Speaking of speed...

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.870
What's the fastest you
renegades have traveled?

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.830
Accelerating feels good, doesn't it?

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.290
TL Note: 60 mph or almost 30 m/s
The other day, I reached 100 km/h,

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.670
for the first time on the freeway!

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.420
Oh my goodness, that's adorable!

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.760
What about you, Onsa-chan?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.050
Jeez.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.840
Bragging about your top speed?

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.390
It's so childish.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.600
But, let's see...

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.680
If I were to bury the needle on my speedometer,

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.650
TL Note: 85 mph or almost 40 m/s
it'd go all the way to 140 km/h on my Serow.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.320
140 km/h?! Amazing!

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.530
That'd only happen if her meter broke.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.490
She's just lying to show off.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.240
What about you, Rin?

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.620
How fast have you gone?

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.790
Um...

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.620
Um...

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.380
TL Note: 125 mph or 55 m/s
200 km/h, something like that.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.880
What? That's impossible.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.840
You're such a buzzkill.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.260
We don't know for sure whether
or not she has lied about that or not.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:49.510
Why don't we test that fact at the
Minowa Test Track in Tokachi?

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.350
Ah fine! It was 100 km/h!

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.600
Just like any safe driver!

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:54.190
Safe
Dri-
ving

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.060
Look!
Safe
Dri-
ving

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:55.350
Safe
Dri-
ving

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.110
All these "safe driving" charms!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.070
Wow, disgusting.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.400
It's charming to see schoolgirls
boasting about their top speeds.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:07.740
But with us in the 200 km/h club...

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.160
Motorcycles are all about cornering.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.580
Oh I forgot...

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.460
Here, a gift for you, Rin-chan!

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:21.750
How did you get a Suzuki Rider's Holy Grail?

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:21.800
Su
zu
ki
How did you get a Suzuki Rider's Holy Grail?

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:22.130
Su
zu
ki

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.670
Someone gave it to me when
I helped him in Aomori.
Su
zu
ki

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:24.720
Someone gave it to me when
I helped him in Aomori.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:28.390
But I already have a knock-

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.970
This is an original!

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.720
It's not a knock-off!

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.060
I'll take it! Yay!

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.230
That man from back then

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.900
called it "The Immortality Cup".

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.650
I'm sure it'll protect you, Rin-chan!

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.540
Today's Route: Straight North!

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.250
TL Note: About 20 bucks (16 euros)
I made a one-night reservation
at some cheap hotel for 2000 yen.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.590
I'm very much looking
forward to see this cheap hotel.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.260
Here it is! The long straight road
that's streches to the horizon!

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:07.680
A mountain road would be nice too,

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.760
but in Hokkaido, straight
roads are more exciting!

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.850
Ah, my shoelace is undone.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.770
Hey guys, everyone stop, Rin's sh-

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.360
I'll catch up with you guys
later, so just keep going.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.690
Okay.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:24.570
Try not to take long alright?

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.910
It's so tempting to speed
on a road like this one.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.950
You shouldn't do that.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.540
You're such a square, Rin.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.790
Hey, guys, look.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.250
Over there— There's a—

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:45.380
They're finally out of range.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.420
But just to be sure,

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.760
Shaggy's stupid!

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.430
All right.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.560
Behind,

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:57.480
in front,

00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.480
above...

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.440
Just for a bit...

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.150
Just for a bit.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.940
Go!

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.200
Top speed challenge!

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.490
Show them your power!

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.790
More! More!

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.290
Howl even louder!

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.620
I am the wind. I am freedom.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.040
I am, I am...

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.960
I am God!

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.840
Foxes!

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:37.220
Your dad illness is called echinococcosis.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.560
It appears he caught it from the red foxes.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:40.480
It's a parasite.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:42.060
Rin...

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.230
Papa! Papa!

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:47.980
All because I saved those red foxes, I...

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.320
If you see a fox on the road,

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.610
don't hesitate and run it over!!

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.120
If I try to avoid hitting the foxes,

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.410
my brakes will lock up and I'll crash.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:01.500
Run them over! Run them over!

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:06.040
It's your fault for coming out on the road!

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.220
Damn it!

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:14.300
Stop already!

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:23.980
Just run away already!

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.600
Shoo, shoo.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.520
You shouldn't be near humans.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.150
You'll give me echinococcus.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.460
I'm so glad...

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.380
I'm glad I saved the foxes...

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:57.090
I'm really glad.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.850
Hey Rin, how'd that Top Speed Challenge go?

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.020
As if I'd do something like that!

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.020
Alright, fine.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:08.650
Don't be so mad about it.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.230
Well, this is Hokkaido.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:14.360
It doesn't matter if you're flying,

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.700
or riding.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.490
You'll always end up here.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.370
Now let's go relax.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:25.000
TL Note: The northern most part of Hokkaido
I wonder what Soya Misaki is like?

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:28.420
TL Note: Almost the same amount in yards
It might even be a hundred-meter-tall cliff.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:32.000
I don't even know, but
I guess we'll find out.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.090
You think we'll make it before sundown?

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.590
Ain't a problem!

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.430
I'm so hungry.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.220
It's already noon?

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.890
My butt hurts.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.350
Let's take a break, then.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.440
Hurry!

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.530
It appears that the sun is already setting.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:57.990
All because I rested for so long...

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.620
The sun's already past the mountains.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.040
Wait please!

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:11.420
We're here!

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.500
We're at Soya Misaki!

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.300
We made it.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:18.550
Northernmost
point of Japan

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:22.470
We didn't just make it,
we made it at the best time!
Northernmost
point of Japan

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:25.560
This is my first time seeing The Sea of Japan.
Northernmost
point of Japan

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:25.600
This is my first time seeing The Sea of Japan.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:30.150
I guess we can't go even
further with our motorcycles.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.480
Yeah, since it's the endpoint.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.780
From here, every road leads back home.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.950
Why don't we take a commemorative
photo before the sun sets?

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.280
Good idea! Let's take one!

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:41.740
Huh?

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.450
That woman over there...

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.290
She looks so lonely.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.290
Should we ask her to move for a bit?

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:49.040
Don't.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:53.540
A lone woman gazing across the sea.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:55.380
It's too much to ask.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.460
I can't ask her to move.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:02.430
Rin, I'm glad you came with us.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.010
What brought that up suddenly?

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.390
Even when you think
you understand others,

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.480
you can never see yourself.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:09.690
What do you mean by that.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:10.730
Huh?

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:13.270
The woman from before is gone.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:15.440
Oh, no!

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.860
Takkun, you idiot!

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.030
Don't do it!
Takkun, you idiot!

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.860
She was rejected by a boy,

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:23.160
so she's doing a bike dive from Soya Misaki.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.830
Your life is important.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.080
Your parents are going to cry!

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:30.160
After that, there's a 100 meter drop!

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:34.080
Oh... Maybe not.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:36.500
Ow...

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.960
What the hell were you trying to do...

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:39.420
Ow...
What the hell were you trying to do...

